whatafailure-by-yeoldelaptopsposse for Debian
---------------------------------------------

Upstream only ships prebuilt executables (Linux x86-64, Windows, macOS).
The Linux executable yo04_lnx is installed unmodified in
/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/whatafailure-by-yeoldelaptopsposse/ and run
by the launcher /usr/bin/whatafailure-by-yeoldelaptopsposse.

The executable was stripped of its section headers to fit in 4 KB, so
dpkg-shlibdeps cannot read its symbols and produces no dependency: the
runtime libraries (libc6, libGL, libGLU, freeglut, SDL 1.2) are listed
by hand in debian/control. It asks for libglut.so.3, provided by a link
to libglut.so.3.12 (freeglut 3.x) in the executable directory. SDL 1.2
comes from sdl12-compat (libsdl1.2debian >= 1.2.60, or libsdl1.2-compat
in its private sdl12-compat/ directory on older distributions).

executable seems to be compiled for an unknown distribution (no section
headers, no compiler identification left in the file; ELF ABI note:
GNU/Linux 2.6.15)

Source files:
-------------
none listed (section headers removed)

